# Editor UI design system

Read `DESIGN.md` before changing any colour, font, spacing, radius, or shadow.

## Colour

Use colours only through CSS custom properties defined in `:root`. No raw hex or rgb elsewhere in `styles.css`.

```css
:root {
  --color-primary: #F54E00;
  --color-secondary: #E6E5E0;
  --color-tertiary: #65AFE0;
  --color-surface: #F2F1ED;
  --color-on-surface: #000000;
  --color-button-bg: #26251E;
  --color-button-fg: #F7F7F4;
}
```

## Type

```css
--font-sans: "Geist", system-ui, "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
--font-mono: "Geist Mono", ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
```

Set headline weight to 400 with the tight tracking in `DESIGN.md`. Set body size to 14 to 16px and line-height to 1.5.

Geist and Geist Mono are the stand-ins for CursorGothic and Berkeley Mono (SIL OFL). Do not bundle Cursor's proprietary fonts. Font files land with the restyle.

## Interpretation

Treat the 1 to 5px spacing scale and the 1 to 2.5px radius scale in `DESIGN.md` as hairlines and borders. Lay the UI out on a 4px grid.

Read the sample button radius `3.35544e+07px` as a pill (`9999px`).

Use the breakpoints 1280, 900, and 768.

## Done

Run the `verify-design` skill before claiming UI work done.
